\f2\fs26 She is the one example of a person with ethics.\'a0 Compared to the rest of her colleagues she is a saint - she rarely (if ever) diverts from protocol and sticks to the letter of the law.\'a0 She had managed to get to a high rank, but her inflexible ethics is the cause of friction between her and the rest of the cops, including higher ranking cops.\'a0 Because she is not corrupt, she is not considered trustworthy - it is only her ability as a cop and her investigative excellence that has allowed her to remain in the cops.\'a0 When she crosses paths with the Chanta, Sarah and the Elvi, she realises\'a0that doing the morally correct thing all of the time is not always the best way to achieve a result.\'a0 She sees that the world is not as black and white it seems - she allows herself to stray from protocol where the Elvi are involved.\'a0\'a0\cf3 \cb1 \
\
\cf3 \cb4 She has the opportunity to killed a reviled murderer, but takes the high road and does not kill him, but arrests him.\'a0 As it turns out she should have killed him as her decision to act morally comes back to bite her on the arse.\'a0\cf3 \cb1 \
\
\cf3 \cb4 She hates Chanta, but I think it is because she might be a lesbian and wants Sarah or it may be that she still has some of the Airborne v Cloudborne predjudices.\'a0 If she is a lesbian she will end up with Dr Logan.}